{"parentUuid":"9e78b25c-33a0-48e0-9a5a-d55c0532bb81","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"mcp__scheduled-tasks__run_scheduled_task","description":"Run an existing scheduled task once, right now — the same as the user clicking \"Run now\" on the task. taskId must be an exact ID from list_scheduled_tasks.\n\nThe run starts as a NEW Claude Code session in the task's working folder with the task's stored prompt, permission mode, and the tool approvals the user already granted that task; it spends the user's usage like any session. Use it when the user asks to run, trigger, test, or re-run a scheduled task now — not to work around a schedule the user set. Refused when the task is disabled, has been deleted, or already has a run in progress.\n\nReturns the new run's session id. The session appears a few seconds later; follow it with mcp__ccd_session_mgmt__get_session or list_events, or call list_task_runs.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"taskId":{"type":"string","description":"The exact ID of the task to run (from list_scheduled_tasks)."}},"required":["taskId"],"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5b27f097-3432-48ec-b6b0-1b6be7b9c301","timestamp":"2026-11-25T21:22:00.064Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise","sessionId":"c2adecd8-a1fc-4e82-9512-79ed47bbae43","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"hidden-dancing-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"5b27f097-3432-48ec-b6b0-1b6be7b9c301","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQM8HAWuPHRLxA7wRgxy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5018,"cache_read_input_tokens":289336,"output_tokens":1860,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":326},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5018,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1860,"cache_read_input_tokens":289336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5018},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3811,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"ca7f7ed4-ea3b-454e-9fa6-d676ed902156","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChQM8Gw843D1v3D3QN2hr","requestRef":"803603af-cde6-438f-9a18-c219ff853485","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"16b39968-4135-4a45-bf42-eef05d916f37","timestamp":"2026-11-25T21:22:00.064Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise","sessionId":"c2adecd8-a1fc-4e82-9512-79ed47bbae43","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"hidden-dancing-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"16b39968-4135-4a45-bf42-eef05d916f37","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQM8HAWuPHRLxA7wRgxy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EHaZJig2iWta3UL8K4empd","name":"mcp__scheduled-tasks__create_scheduled_task","input":{"taskId":"jusprin1-pending-moves-daily","title":"JusPrin 1 subscriptions to end (daily)","description":"Daily read-only check: which JusPrin 1 subscribers moved to a JusPrin 2 loyalty plan and need their JusPrin 1 subscription ended at term end","cronExpression":"0 8 * * *","notifyOnCompletion":true,"prompt":"Daily check: which paying JusPrin 1 subscribers have moved to JusPrin 2 and now need their JusPrin 1 subscription ended. This is READ ONLY. Never change anything in Chargebee, the database or anywhere else. Kenneth ends each subscription himself.\n\nBackground: on 25 Nov 2026, the 18 paying JusPrin 1 subscribers were emailed a one-time code. The code moves them to a JusPrin 2 Hobby \"loyalty\" plan at their old price, with the first period free. The email promised that their JusPrin 1 subscription \"runs to the end of the time you've already paid for, then stops, so you never pay for both\". Nothing ends it automatically. If a JusPrin 1 subscription reaches its renewal date before Kenneth ends it, the person is charged twice.\n\nSteps:\n1. Switch gcloud to the agent account:\n   gcloud config set account ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com\n2. Run the command with the Bash tool. Set dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true, because the sandbox proxy breaks TLS:\n   /Users/kenneth/Projects/ops/tsd/prod/run_django_mgmt_cmd.sh jusprin1_pending_moves\n3. Read the output:\n   - Each tab-separated line before the summary is a subscription to end. It gives the address, whether that address is verified on Obico, the Obico user id, the JusPrin 1 subscription id with its plan and renewal date, the JusPrin 2 user id, and the JusPrin 2 plan.\n   - An optional section \"Loyalty plans with no JusPrin 1 subscription at the same address\" lists JusPrin 2 loyalty plans that couldn't be matched to a JusPrin 1 subscription. That is usually someone who signed up with a different address.\n   - The last line is the summary: \"N live JusPrin 1 subscriptions; X to end at the end of the term; Y already ending; Z loyalty plans unmatched.\"\n4. Decide what to report:\n   - If X is 0 and Z is 0, end quietly. Reply with one line: the summary line and today's date. Send no notification.\n   - Otherwise, send Kenneth a push notification (PushNotification tool) if it is available. Keep it short, and use user ids and subscription ids, not email addresses. For example: \"2 JusPrin 1 subscriptions to end at term end: sub AzZ… renews 2026-12-07 …\". Put any subscription that renews within 3 days first, marked URGENT.\n   - Then give the full details in your reply, in plain sentences:\n     - Each subscription to end, with its renewal date and how many days remain.\n     - Each row marked \"UNVERIFIED on Obico\". Say Kenneth should confirm with the person before ending it, because the address match isn't proven.\n     - Each JusPrin 2 plan marked \"(NOT a loyalty plan)\". That person bought a regular plan. Kenneth decides what to do.\n     - Each unmatched loyalty plan. That person may have used a different address, and Kenneth may need to reply to them to find their JusPrin 1 subscription.\n   - Remind Kenneth how to end a subscription: in Obico's Chargebee site (not the jusprinv2 site), cancel the subscription \"at the end of the current term\". Never cancel immediately, because ending it now writes a refundable credit for the unused time.\n5. If the command fails, prints anything else, or the gcloud/kubectl step errors, report the exact command and error. Don't guess at the result, and send a push notification saying the daily check failed.\n\nAfter 31 March 2027: the codes expired on 28 February 2027. Add one line telling Kenneth that once X has been 0 for a while, this task can be turned off."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5018,"cache_read_input_tokens":289336,"output_tokens":1860,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":326},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5018,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1860,"cache_read_input_tokens":289336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5018},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":12911,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EHaZJig2iWta3UL8K4empd":{"taskId":"jusprin1-pending-moves-daily","title":"JusPrin 1 subscriptions to end (daily)","description":"Daily read-only check: which JusPrin 1 subscribers moved to a JusPrin 2 loyalty plan and need their JusPrin 1 subscription ended at term end","cronExpression":"0 8 * * *","notifyOnCompletion":true,"prompt":"Daily check: which paying JusPrin 1 subscribers have moved to JusPrin 2 and now need their JusPrin 1 subscription ended. This is READ ONLY. Never change anything in Chargebee, the database or anywhere else. Kenneth ends each subscription himself.\n\nBackground: on 25 Nov 2026, the 18 paying JusPrin 1 subscribers were emailed a one-time code. The code moves them to a JusPrin 2 Hobby \"loyalty\" plan at their old price, with the first period free. The email promised that their JusPrin 1 subscription \"runs to the end of the time you've already paid for, then stops, so you never pay for both\". Nothing ends it automatically. If a JusPrin 1 subscription reaches its renewal date before Kenneth ends it, the person is charged twice.\n\nSteps:\n1. Switch gcloud to the agent account:\n   gcloud config set account ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com\n2. Run the command with the Bash tool. Set dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true, because the sandbox proxy breaks TLS:\n   /Users/kenneth/Projects/ops/tsd/prod/run_django_mgmt_cmd.sh jusprin1_pending_moves\n3. Read the output:\n   - Each tab-separated line before the summary is a subscription to end. It gives the address, whether that address is verified on Obico, the Obico user id, the JusPrin 1 subscription id with its plan and renewal date, the JusPrin 2 user id, and the JusPrin 2 plan.\n   - An optional section \"Loyalty plans with no JusPrin 1 subscription at the same address\" lists JusPrin 2 loyalty plans that couldn't be matched to a JusPrin 1 subscription. That is usually someone who signed up with a different address.\n   - The last line is the summary: \"N live JusPrin 1 subscriptions; X to end at the end of the term; Y already ending; Z loyalty plans unmatched.\"\n4. Decide what to report:\n   - If X is 0 and Z is 0, end quietly. Reply with one line: the summary line and today's date. Send no notification.\n   - Otherwise, send Kenneth a push notification (PushNotification tool) if it is available. Keep it short, and use user ids and subscription ids, not email addresses. For example: \"2 JusPrin 1 subscriptions to end at term end: sub AzZ… renews 2026-12-07 …\". Put any subscription that renews within 3 days first, marked URGENT.\n   - Then give the full details in your reply, in plain sentences:\n     - Each subscription to end, with its renewal date and how many days remain.\n     - Each row marked \"UNVERIFIED on Obico\". Say Kenneth should confirm with the person before ending it, because the address match isn't proven.\n     - Each JusPrin 2 plan marked \"(NOT a loyalty plan)\". That person bought a regular plan. Kenneth decides what to do.\n     - Each unmatched loyalty plan. That person may have used a different address, and Kenneth may need to reply to them to find their JusPrin 1 subscription.\n   - Remind Kenneth how to end a subscription: in Obico's Chargebee site (not the jusprinv2 site), cancel the subscription \"at the end of the current term\". Never cancel immediately, because ending it now writes a refundable credit for the unused time.\n5. If the command fails, prints anything else, or the gcloud/kubectl step errors, report the exact command and error. Don't guess at the result, and send a push notification saying the daily check failed.\n\nAfter 31 March 2027: the codes expired on 28 February 2027. Add one line telling Kenneth that once X has been 0 for a while, this task can be turned off."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ca7f7ed4-ea3b-454e-9fa6-d676ed902156","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChQM8Gw843D1v3D3QN2hr","requestRef":"803603af-cde6-438f-9a18-c219ff853485","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"85b0aa65-f84f-4048-8512-96ef51640158","timestamp":"2026-11-25T21:22:12.976Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise","sessionId":"c2adecd8-a1fc-4e82-9512-79ed47bbae43","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"hidden-dancing-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
