{"parentUuid":"e98fcf9b-a810-43c8-b37f-c669d7861099","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQMLWeiP5uLTyCLpudnw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":789,"cache_read_input_tokens":299578,"output_tokens":813,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":93},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":789,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":813,"cache_read_input_tokens":299578,"cache_creation_input_tokens":789,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":789},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1215,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"55ad1e7b-a507-4ea7-8a57-a69879937e10","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChQMLWQ68KfBNRGPWwzfu","requestRef":"d458737f-9baa-42f0-9551-4ab979585a5c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"f04768f6-2389-42e1-925c-80e6bc9acf19","timestamp":"2026-11-25T21:24:43.333Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/jusprin2-email-data","sessionId":"c2adecd8-a1fc-4e82-9512-79ed47bbae43","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"jusprin-dev","slug":"hidden-dancing-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"f04768f6-2389-42e1-925c-80e6bc9acf19","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQMLWeiP5uLTyCLpudnw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QRLG2Wugt3hiZN1mMNaRrv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/recipient-count-names-who-is-left-out.md","content":"---\nname: recipient-count-names-who-is-left-out\ndescription: When reporting who an email goes to, say \"N of M\" and name who is left out and why; re-check exclusions when the plan changes\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nOn 2026-11-25 the code email went to 18 paying JusPrin 1 subscribers. There were 19. One (monthly, renewing 18 Dec, already had a JusPrin 2 account) had been left out of the SendGrid upload under the earlier hand-move plan, to get a separate version after a manual move. When the plan switched to one-time codes, that exclusion was never revisited, and every report said \"all 18\" without saying it was 18 of 19. Kenneth found out from the daily check's \"19 live\" line: \"you didn't bother to tell me?\"\n\n**Why:** a count without its total hides the people dropped. Kenneth reads \"all 18 subscribers\" as \"every subscriber\".\n\n**How to apply:** whenever reporting an audience or a send, say \"N of M\" and name each person left out and why. When a plan changes, go back through every exclusion made under the old plan and check whether it still holds, before asking for a send. Related: [[report-outcomes-not-obstacles]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":789,"cache_read_input_tokens":299578,"output_tokens":813,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":93},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":789,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":813,"cache_read_input_tokens":299578,"cache_creation_input_tokens":789,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":789},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":4601,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QRLG2Wugt3hiZN1mMNaRrv":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/recipient-count-names-who-is-left-out.md","content":"---\nname: recipient-count-names-who-is-left-out\ndescription: When reporting who an email goes to, say \"N of M\" and name who is left out and why; re-check exclusions when the plan changes\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nOn 2026-11-25 the code email went to 18 paying JusPrin 1 subscribers. There were 19. One (monthly, renewing 18 Dec, already had a JusPrin 2 account) had been left out of the SendGrid upload under the earlier hand-move plan, to get a separate version after a manual move. When the plan switched to one-time codes, that exclusion was never revisited, and every report said \"all 18\" without saying it was 18 of 19. Kenneth found out from the daily check's \"19 live\" line: \"you didn't bother to tell me?\"\n\n**Why:** a count without its total hides the people dropped. Kenneth reads \"all 18 subscribers\" as \"every subscriber\".\n\n**How to apply:** whenever reporting an audience or a send, say \"N of M\" and name each person left out and why. When a plan changes, go back through every exclusion made under the old plan and check whether it still holds, before asking for a send. Related: [[report-outcomes-not-obstacles]].\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"55ad1e7b-a507-4ea7-8a57-a69879937e10","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChQMLWQ68KfBNRGPWwzfu","requestRef":"d458737f-9baa-42f0-9551-4ab979585a5c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","