{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c2adecd8-a1fc-4e82-9512-79ed47bbae43","hash":"162560551625e4ef587b8c5f0861209ad6c20c78e290b6227da4bda98c770583","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QRLG2Wugt3hiZN1mMNaRrv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/recipient-count-names-who-is-left-out.md","content":"---\nname: recipient-count-names-who-is-left-out\ndescription: When reporting who an email goes to, say \"N of M\" and name who is left out and why; re-check exclusions when the plan changes\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nOn 2026-11-25 the code email went to 18 paying JusPrin 1 subscribers. There were 19. One (monthly, renewing 18 Dec, already had a JusPrin 2 account) had been left out of the SendGrid upload under the earlier hand-move plan, to get a separate version after a manual move. When the plan switched to one-time codes, that exclusion was never revisited, and every report said \"all 18\" without saying it was 18 of 19. Kenneth found out from the daily check's \"19 live\" line: \"you didn't bother to tell me?\"\n\n**Why:** a count without its total hides the people dropped. Kenneth reads \"all 18 subscribers\" as \"every subscriber\".\n\n**How to apply:** whenever reporting an audience or a send, say \"N of M\" and name each person left out and why. When a plan changes, go back through every exclusion made under the old plan and check whether it still holds, before asking for a send. Related: [[report-outcomes-not-obstacles]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017GAy1JxFLfVnhyPbGCw7aM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory && echo '- [Name who is left out](recipient-count-names-who-is-left-out.md) — \"N of M\" for every send; re-check old exclusions when the plan changes (19th JusPrin 1 subscriber missed