"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/jusprin2-email-data","sessionId":"c2adecd8-a1fc-4e82-9512-79ed47bbae43","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"hidden-dancing-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"6b924bab-18f1-4c70-8522-a8e80906f7c0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3a3c9c0d-d32f-4951-8247-11876ce7ec91","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ahWkYA45qQbV3gw2gJ2bT","type":"tool_result","content":"                                SENT 2026-11-18 04:33-04:34 UTC (Kenneth: \"send batch 5 now\"); all four groups added to\n                                jusprin2_sent_all.csv as \"5 (b5a_beta)\" etc. batch5_arms_sent_2026-11-17.csv = the 4,110 with arm.\n                                In SendGrid (only these 4,110 are contacts): list 32200594; segments 14034017 (b5a) and 14034019 (b5b),\n                                2,055 each; draft campaigns 22635622 (b5a: sender \"Kenneth from JusPrin\", subject \"JusPrin 2 is here\")\n                                and 22635626 (b5b: sender \"Kenneth from Obico\", subject \"Meet JusPrin 2, from the team behind Obico\"),\n                                category jusprin2-batch5, unsubscribe group 8150. Test copies checked 2026-11-17.\n                                Delete these contacts before 2026-12-01 (storage is billed on the month's peak).\nbatch5_email_a.txt/.html, batch5_email_b.txt/.html  the two emails as built in SendGrid.\n                                2026-11-17, before sending (Kenneth): the \"No AI account? Sign up in the app for 500 free credits\"\n                                sentence became its own paragraph in both emails, \"Join the JusPrin Cloud beta for 500 free credits...\",\n                                to test whether a beta offer draws makers in.\n                                Then (Kenneth: \"let's do 4 groups\") each group was split again by salted hash\n                                ('jusprin2-batch5-beta-2026-11-17'+email) into beta / no-beta halves; jusprin2_arm is now\n                                b5a_beta 1,028, b5a_nobeta 1,027, b5b_beta 1,028, b5b_nobeta 1,027\n                                (batch5_candidates_4groups_2026-11-17.csv; batch5_upload_4groups.csv relabelled the SendGrid contacts).\n                                No-beta paragraph: \"Sign up for JusPrin Cloud in the app for 500 free credits, with no card needed.\n                                JusPrin Cloud is the AI service we run for you, ...\" (batch5_email_{a,b}_nobeta.*).\n                                Segments 14034071 b5a_beta, 14034072 b5a_nobeta, 14034073 b5b_beta, 14034074 b5b_nobeta\n                                (old 14034017 b5a / 14034019 b5b now count 0). Campaigns: 22635622 5a beta, 22635765 5a no-beta,\n                                22635626 5b beta, 22635770 5b no-beta.\n                                Then (Kenneth: one word was too easy to miss) the beta emails got a bold first line,\n                                \"You're invited to the JusPrin Cloud beta. Join it in the app and get 500 free credits...\", and a\n                                P.S. under the signature: \"P.S. The JusPrin Cloud beta is open now. Join it in the app for 500 free\n                                credits.\" The no-beta emails were left as they were. batch5_email_{a,b}.* hold the beta text.\n                                Lesson: a SendGrid editor tab left open on a draft keeps saving its old copy over later edits.\n                                Then (Kenneth: the YouTube preview card Gmail shows under the email was missing) the video link was\n                                put on its own line with clicktracking=off in all four HTML versions. SendGrid click tracking rewrites\n                                links to ct.sendgrid.net/ls/click, and Gmail shows the playable card only for a real youtube.com link.\n                                Batch 4 had tracked video links too, so it had no card either. Video clicks are now NOT counted in\n                                SendGrid click totals for batch 5 (the download and announcement links still are), the same in all\n                                four groups. Test copies of all four checked 2026-11-17: direct YouTube link, right beta / no-beta text.\n\nbatch5_opens_clicks_2026-11-24.csv  who opened / clicked batch 5, one row per person, with arm and SendGrid's last_emailed,\n                                last_opened and last_clicked (UTC), read 2026-11-24 about 6.5 days after the send.\n                                1,447 people: opened b5a_beta 380, b5a_nobeta 378, b5b_beta 351, b5b_nobeta 328;\n                                clicked 9 / 9 / 8 / 6 (download or announcement link; the video link was untracked).\n                                10 clickers have no open recorded (images blocked). Every row matches batch5_arms_sent_2026-11-17.csv.\n                                The batch 5 contacts were still in SendGrid on 2026-11-24 (only they are; batches 1-4 are gone).\n                                Still to do: delete them before 2026-12-01.\n\nJusPrin 1 subscribers (2026-11-24, NOT SENT):\n    1448 batch5_opens_clicks_2026-11-24.csv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0aa8b4d0-36d4-49c0-9221-e064b0b2887f","timestamp":"2026-11-25T23:56:07.073Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"                                SENT 2026-11-18 04:33-04:34 UTC (Kenneth: \"send batch 5 now\"); all four groups added to\n                                jusprin2_sent_all.csv as \"5 (b5a_beta)\" etc. batch5_arms_sent_2026-11-17.csv = the 4,110 with arm.\n                                In SendGrid (only these 4,110 are contacts): list 32200594; segments 14034017 (b5a) and 14034019 (b5b),\n                                2,055 each; draft campaigns 22635622 (b5a: sender \"Kenneth from JusPrin\", subject \"JusPrin 2 is here\")\n                                and 22635626 (b5b: sender \"Kenneth from Obico\", subject \"Meet JusPrin 2, from the team behind Obico\"),\n                                category jusprin2-batch5, unsubscribe group 8150. Test copies checked 2026-11-17.\n                                Delete these contacts before 2026-12-01 (storage is billed on the month's peak).\nbatch5_email_a.txt/.html, batch5_email_b.txt/.html  the two emails as built in SendGrid.\n                                2026-11-17, before sending (Kenneth): the \"No AI account? Sign up in the app for 500 free credits\"\n                                sentence became its own paragraph in both emails, \"Join the JusPrin Cloud beta for 500 free credits...\",\n                                to test whether a beta offer draws makers in.\n                                Then (Kenneth: \"let's do 4 groups\") each group was split again by salted hash\n                                ('jusprin2-batch5-beta-2026-11-17'+email) into beta / no-beta halves; jusprin2_arm is now\n                                b5a_beta 1,028, b5a_nobeta 1,027, b5b_beta 1,028, b5b_nobeta 1,027\n                                (batch5_candidates_4groups_2026-11-17.csv; batch5_upload_4groups.csv relabelled the SendGrid contacts).\n                                No-beta paragraph: \"Sign up for JusPrin Cloud in the app for 500 free credits, with no card needed.\n                                JusPrin Cloud is the AI service we run for you, ...\" (batch5_email_{a,b}_nobeta.*).\n                                Segments 14034071 b5a_beta, 14034072 b5a_nobeta, 14034073 b5b_beta, 14034074 b5b_nobeta\n                                (old 14034017 b5a / 14034019 b5b now count 0). Campaigns: 22635622 5a beta, 22635765 5a no-beta,\n                                22635626 5b beta, 22635770 5b no-beta.\n                                Then (Kenneth: one word was too easy to miss) the beta emails got a bold first line,\n                                \"You're invited to the JusPrin Cloud beta. Join it in the app and get 500 free credits...\", and a\n                                P.S. under the signature: \"P.S. The JusPrin Cloud beta is open now. Join it in the app for 500 free\n                                credits.\" The no-beta emails were left as they were. batch5_email_{a,b}.* hold the beta text.\n                                Lesson: a SendGrid editor tab left open on a draft keeps saving its old copy over later edits.\n                                Then (Kenneth: the YouTube preview card Gmail shows under the email was missing) the video link was\n                                put on its own line with clicktracking=off in all four HTML versions. SendGrid click tracking rewrites\n                                links to ct.sendgrid.net/ls/click, and Gmail shows the playable card only for a real youtube.com link.\n                                Batch 4 had tracked video links too, so it had no card either. Video clicks are now NOT counted in\n                                SendGrid click totals for batch 5 (the download and announcement links still are), the same in all\n                                four groups. Test copies of all four checked 2026-11-17: direct YouTube link, right beta / no-beta text.\n\nbatch5_opens_clicks_2026-11-24.csv  who opened / clicked batch 5, one row per person, with arm and SendGrid's last_emailed,\n                                last_opened and last_clicked (UTC), read 2026-11-24 about 6.5 days after the send.\n                                1,447 people: opened b5a_beta 380, b5a_nobeta 378, b5b_beta 351, b5b_nobeta 328;\n                                clicked 9 / 9 / 8 / 6 (download or announcement link; the video link was untracked).\n                                10 clickers have no open recorded (images blocked). Every row matches batch5_arms_sent_2026-11-17.csv.\n                                The batch 5 contacts were still in SendGrid on 2026-11-24 (only they are; batches 1-4 are gone).\n                                Still to do: delete them before 2026-12-01.\n\nJusPrin 1 subscribers (2026-11-24, NOT SENT):\n    1448 batch5_opens_clicks_2026-11-24.csv","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssi